[C#m]They say every [D]distance [E]is not [A]near
[A]So I remember every [Bm]face
[C#m]Of every [D]man who [E]put me [A]here
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]I see my light come [Bm]shining
[C#m]From the [D]west unto [E]the [A]east
[A]Any day now, Any day now,
[C#m]I shall [D]be [A]released
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
They say every man needs protection.
They say that every man must fall.
Yet I swear I see my reflection,
Someplace so high above this wall.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Down here next to me in this lonely crowd
